      "mergeID": "637bc28b1d7db14a4c8a075f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When hovering over a button in the new menu, e.g. the \"invite to instance\" button, new submenus are positioned slighly above the menu plane, but the pointer is still rendered all the way down to the menu plane, which creates a weird effect for VR users to look at. This is also the case for buttons that elevate away from the menu plane when hovering over them, but the pointer still stays at the menu plane. The result is an unrealistic view that is uncomfortable to look at in VR.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Menu pointer is rendered at wrong distance for submenus and hovering buttons",
